                <pb facs="0287" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg267"/>

                <head>French rifled guns.</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the Editor of the Times:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In your leading article of to-day upon
                    iron-clad ships there occurs a mistake, which, though perhaps obvious to the
                    initiated, should, I think, be corrected, so that full effect may be given to
                    the otherwise accurate statements made respecting the broadside rifled gun used
                    in the French navy. This gun throws a solid shot of 30 kilogrammes, not 30
                    pounds weight, and may, therefore, be termed a 60-pounder.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
